WEBVTT

00:00:00.293 --> 00:00:07.742
A lot of SQL knowledge transfers across PostgreSQL and Spark SQL, especially core relational patterns.

00:00:07.742 --> 00:00:11.487
But dialect differences remain.

00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:20.132
Date functions, file-reading commands, table creation, and temporary view syntax can differ.

00:00:20.132 --> 00:00:26.202
A strong learner separates the relational idea from the engine-specific syntax used to express it.

00:00:26.202 --> 00:00:35.417
Many relational ideas transfer directly to Spark SQL: NULL semantics, date arithmetic, CTEs, joins, grouping,

00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:36.737
and windows.

00:00:36.737 --> 00:00:45.477
Syntax details may differ, but the same reasoning about grain, missingness, and cardinality still applies.

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:53.120
Portability is easiest when the business rule is clear before dialect-specific tuning.
